course: dictionary
lesson: 7654
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Promotion is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because the context tells you which meaning the writer chose. «A promotion is a move up to a more senior job in the same organisation, usually with more responsibility and more pay.» Here the clues are job, responsibility and pay, so promotion means a move up at work.
explain: The same word can mean something different in a shop. A sign that says «buy one, get one free» promotion is about a special offer that makes people want to buy. The clues are buy, free and the shop, so this promotion is a deal, not a job. Always ask: what does the sentence seem to be about?
explain: In sport, promotion means a team moves up to a higher league. In health lessons, the promotion of good health means helping good health to happen or grow. Try your chosen meaning in the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Promotion has four meanings: a move up at work, a special offer, a team moving up a league, and helping something to grow.
fact: «Promotion» in a shop usually means a special offer, such as «20% off».
fact: «Promotion» in sport means a team moving up to a higher league.
fact: «Promotion» with «of» can mean helping something to happen or grow, as in «the promotion of good health».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «A promotion is a move up to a more senior job in the same organisation.» What does promotion mean here? | Special offer on a shop item | Helping good health to grow | A team moving down a league | *Moving up to a better job
exercise: A shop sign says «buy one, get one free» promotion. What does promotion mean here? | Moving up to a higher job | Helping something to grow | *Special offer to make people buy | A team moving up a league
exercise: Mia reads that a team won promotion to the top league. What does promotion mean here? | Buying one thing and getting one free | Helping good health to grow | Moving up to a better job at work | *A team moving up to a higher league
test: In «the promotion of good health», what does promotion mean? | Moving up to a better job | A team moving up a league | Special offer in a shop | *Helping something to happen or grow
test: Ben reads, «Grown-ups wait on probation, then hope for a pay rise or a promotion.» What is a promotion here? | *A move up to a more senior job | A team winning a cup | A cheap price in a shop | An advert on the radio
exam: A shop sign says «3 for the price of 2» on toys that cost £2 each. What do you really pay for three toys? | £2 | *£4 | £6 | £3
